// Title: APT PRIVATELOG Image Load Pattern
// Sigma ID: 33a2d1dd-f3b0-40bd-8baf-7974468927cc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-09-07 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1055
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects an image load pattern as seen when a tool named PRIVATELOG is used and rarely observed
//   under legitimate circumstances
// False positives:
//   - Rarely observed
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20210901184449/https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2021/09/unknown-actor-using-clfs-log-files-for-stealth.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules-emerging-threats/2021/TA/PRIVATELOG/image_load_usp_svchost_clfsw32.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\clfsw32.dll"
